{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the hosted agent witness script at head f25b44a3, tree at the note's checkpoint plus the note and manifest, for request 7ba98c19 and review request f829024a. Verdict: APPROVED FOR THE RUN ONLY. Do not land this head. It meets no done-when item, and the head that adds the run's evidence needs its own review.\n\nThis approval is the one that planner decision b328327d waits for. It covers the script's design and its safety on a deployed Worker. It says nothing about whether the live run will succeed.\n\n## Your six questions\n\n1. **The ledger: it holds the rule together with the structure, and it does not hold it alone.** The stronger evidence is that `agentPhase` takes only a session, a mode and `standInBase`, and a test fixes the imports of `agent.ts`. The ledger then catches a value that a later edit brings in. Its limits are real. The literals are one list for every phase, not a list per phase. `1` and `60` are literals, so any fact equal to them passes. Booleans are not checked. Each of the texts and scope names I read in that list is the script's own word or an alias, so none of them supplies a room fact. Describe the rule that way in the run's report, and do not claim that the ledger proves where each value came from.\n2. **The tool list: enough, with the printed names.** The generic names are exact, and `MCP_TOOL_ADDITIONS` can add only generic names, so any addition stops the run. `agent-tools` prints every name, and every later phase prints the list's digest, so a reader can compare the names with the definitions. One limit: `hostedDefaultTools` reads the policy from the script's checkout, not from the Worker. The run's evidence must therefore show that the deployed commit and this checkout have the same `packages/mcp/src/hosted-tools.ts`, or the deployed list's generic names must be compared by hand.\n3. **The fresh session: `agent-resume` uses nothing else that reaches a room.** It reads the record through the session and signs nothing. It compares two things with the script's memory, `TEXT.body` and the fixed act order in `agent-verify`, and each can only stop the phase. The signing phases also use fixed `idempotencyKey` words, which the ledger exempts. Those words are the script's memory, not the record's. State that in the report, because a model in a new session would have to choose or find its own key.\n4. **A scripted agent: an honest witness of less than the words \"one agent\" can suggest.** It shows that the hosted default tools and the record are enough to run the loop, that the scope holds the order and the signers, and that a person's decision comes from another session. It does not show that a model follows the prompt, or chooses well among 57 tools. The note says this plainly. The request itself asks for a script and names facts and tools, so I accept it for done-when. The final report and any public text must say that a script ran and no model read the prompt. The planner's decision rests on 456f5a3e, which does not say so, so I am telling the planner separately.\n5. **The public output: I found no field that carries a body or a token.** A string must match one of the closed shapes. Those shapes hold no space and no uppercase free text, and the free-form shape stops below 32 token characters and at 48 characters in all. `sha256:` digests can print, and `commentDigest` is one, but the room's texts here are fixed `TEST` words. Non-`LoopStop` errors print only `stopped-unclassified`. One small mismatch: `privateValues` in `main.ts` holds the bearer, its secret and the texts, while `scanPublic`'s comment also names the link. The projection refuses a link's shape first, so nothing leaks, but add the link or correct the comment on the next head.\n6. **The loopback option: closed on the path you asked about.** `local` requires `options.loopback === true`, `http:` and exactly `127.0.0.1`. S1's callers pass no option. The founder adoption in `owner` needs `isLoopback`, and `standInBase` is refused on HTTPS. Beyond that path, `person()` accepts an existing home with no retained plan and writes the plan into it. A real S1 identity sits in `owner`, `agent-a`, `agent-b` or `checker`, so `\u003chome\u003e/person` finds none of them unless someone arranges it on purpose. I do not block on that. Refusing a home with no retained plan outside the `owner` phase would close it, and it costs one condition on the next head.\n\n## What I expect the run's evidence to show\n\n- The public line of all 29 phases, on one Worker version, with that version in the deployment receipt, and no deployment between the first phase and the last.\n- `agent-tools`' names and prompt digest, and the same list check in every later agent phase.\n- `agent-propose` on a real base from the branch's `head`, and `agent-verify`'s order and signers read back from the record.\n- A separate session ID digest for each agent phase, and a real wait in `agent-wait` that ends on the person's `decide`.\n- A scan of the sealed unit for the bearer, its secret, the link and the `TEST` texts. The planner's 404 after closing belongs to the deploy record.\n\nA stop on the live run is a finding, not a failure of this review. A stop after `create` costs a new home and a new room. The runbook says that, and it should also say what happens to the old room's agent.\n\n## Two points to settle by the next head\n\n- **The bearer stays on disk.** The runbook leaves the scratch agent and its bearer in place, and the object keeps the agent's key. A later slice that reopens the endpoint makes that bearer live again. Say in the runbook that the operator deletes the private home after sealing, or revoke the agent's key as a last phase.\n- **Blank-line residue.** `packages/mcp/test/hosted-loop.scope.test.ts` has a blank line inside the checks at line 796 and a misindented line at 812.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. The script reuses S1's modules and forks nothing. No hosted code changes. It keeps the agent's phases away from the operator's input by their signature, and the person's session by a separate home and key.\n\n**Security.** No blocking issue. The bearer file is `0600`, created with `O_EXCL` and `O_NOFOLLOW`. `agentFetch` stops any other address, and it refuses redirects. The agent's list holds no person-only act. Opening the endpoint exposes it for the whole Worker for the length of the run, which is the planner's decision in b328327d.\n\n**Simplification.** Acceptable. `agent.ts` is one long dispatch, but each branch is one phase and reads in the runbook's order. `local-run.mjs` stays out of the gate.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** All of `agent.ts`, `hosted-session.ts`, `hosted-client.ts`, `tool-list.ts`, `public.ts`, `main.ts`, `person.ts`, `plan.ts`, `control.ts`, `words.ts`, `runbook.md`, the note, the native test, and the changes to `identities.ts` and `diagnostics.ts`.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `5b598b3e…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `389a7fb3`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3418 plain and 908 native tests. The diff from there to this head touches only the note and its manifest. `controls/results.json` holds 31 rows, all red by an assertion. `local-run/summary.json` holds 46 entries and no problems. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `examples/repo-in-ai/test/hosted-loop.test.ts` passes 177 of 177. `packages/mcp/test/hosted-loop.scope.test.ts` passes 1 of 1. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged, and `check-kernel-boundary` 127 sources with 0 refusals. The worktree stayed clean.\n- **A live room's base.** S1's `publication.ts` expects a room's head to start at a founding commit, and the native test proposes on a head from its stand-in Git host. From that reading, I expect a live room to hold a base by `agent-propose`. Nothing has shown this on dap-demo, and the creation offer's cohort there may differ from the two cohorts already run.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader. I did not run `local-run.mjs` or any control, or read `local-run.mjs` beyond its stand-ins, or read most of `hosted-loop.test.ts`. No part of this has run on a deployed Worker.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:74e0a17178fe3626d51f0de15b9dea8691560d5d","binding":"assigned","head":"f25b44a34376c65b9e5e4b20ee5596dfaf0a2ab3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:233e64c3fbea12d1118199ddfe108196a3abf23d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d119a5b5f2d732210266a7af507eca2b6fbd3cd0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:233e64c3fbea12d1118199ddfe108196a3abf23d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0b6e21582f9827a54ca113e654528fd381353f8b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:166bc052e40a405387b0e09da994bbdb0c294470, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:20c0303219f9dfd03ef4fc38ba05c4500b5397e1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:233e64c3fbea12d1118199ddfe108196a3abf23d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2659183d052d0731d71b8564cf1e04d13e974f3e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:26d49c768de19247282af94cd33947cd90d45544, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f18480e0be32666310985742d7709e853838a8c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4b3f4aaadd0571521d3ac9f16962a4ce1495bd55, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:57bf35e169cd17b5e9770ecbfc7d15d30e27a4b6, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5d84f1e09f0042d04efe55d0759181a678cd96de, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1